        "answer": "# Gross Domestic Product (GDP)\n\nGDP is the **market value of all the final goods and services produced in a country during a specific time period**. \n\nIt can be calculated using the expenditure approach as:\n$GDP = C + I + G + (X - M)$\nWhere:\n**C** = Consumption\n**I** = Investment\n**G** = Government Expenditure\n**(X - M)** = Exports minus Imports \n\n**Key Points:**\n*   Only **final goods and services** are included to avoid **double counting** of intermediate goods. \n*   It measures goods and services produced **within the country's geographical boundaries** during the specified period. \n*   In India, GDP is measured both annually (for a financial year) and quarterly. \n\n**📘 Source:** Samacheer Kalvi Class 10 Social Science • Gdp"
      },
